# Copy to .env to override the defaults. .env is git-ignored and is never
# packaged into a build.
#
# Loaded by Node's built-in .env parser, so there is no dotenv dependency.

# Where the SQLite database lives. Relative paths resolve from the repository
# root in development, and from the app directory once packaged.
#
# Leave unset to use the defaults:
#   development   <repo>/.data/sales-pro.db
#   packaged      <OS userData>/sales-pro.db
#
# Set it to read a packaged build's real data with `npm run db:studio`:
#   macOS         ~/Library/Application Support/sales-pro/sales-pro.db
#   Windows       %APPDATA%\sales-pro\sales-pro.db
#
# SALES_PRO_DB_PATH=.data/sales-pro.db
